The proposal (@simonbrunel ): 
```js
config: {
  options: {
    datasets[dataset_type]
    plugins[plugin_type]
  }
}
Chart.overrides: {
  [chart_type]: {
    datasets[dataset_type]
    plugins[plugin_type]
  }
}
Chart.defaults: {
  datasets[dataset_type]
  plugins[plugin_type]
}
```

* The chart type defaults are moved from `Chart.defaults.controllers[type]` to `Chart.overrides[type]`
* The dataset type defaults are moved from `Chart.defaults.controllers[type].dataset` to `Chart.defaults.datasets[type]`

This simplifies the fallback logic and adds another advanced configuration dimension, for overriding dataset type defaults per chart type. So you could set defaults for a `line` dataset in a `bar` chart, for example.


